LC 977 — Squares of a Sorted Array
Pattern:Two Pointers

Logic:

Largest square comes from the largest absolute value.
Compare abs(a[l]) and abs(a[r])
Put the larger square at the end
Move that pointer

Algorithm:
l = 0, r = n-1
Compare a[l]² and a[r]²
Put larger one at ans[k]
Move pointer + k--

CODE:
class Solution {
public:
    vector<int> sortedSquares(vector<int>& a) {
        int l=0, r=a.size()-1, k=r;
        vector<int> ans(a.size());
        while (l<=r) {
            if (abs(a[l]) > abs(a[r]))
                ans[k--] = a[l]*a[l++];
            else
                ans[k--] = a[r]*a[r--];
        }
        return ans;
    }
};

a = [-4,-1,0,3,10]

Compare -4²=16 and 10²=100
→ put 100 at end

[-4,-1,0,3,100]

Compare -4²=16 and 3²=9
→ put 16

